From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:34:51 -0400
Subject: D3D11: Expand 3D texture depth in MakeValidSize

When d3d11::MakeValidSize expands sub-block compressed mip dimensions
by levelOffset, also shift requestDepth for 3D textures so the selected
D3D11 mip subresource has mDepth slices.

Test:
    angle_end2end_tests --gtest_filter="*BPTCCompressedTextureTestES3.CompressedTexImage3DSubBlockMipDepth/*"
Bug: b/564064199
Change-Id: I913ba2abcd631714b617ea8d835c9a2bcfb6f36a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8451922
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y): TextureStorage11_2D/Cube constructors
on this ANGLE revision carry an extra zeroMaxLodWorkaround ASSERT next to
the mTextureDepth assignment; the conflict was resolved by keeping that
ASSERT and taking upstream's `mTextureDepth = depth`.

This branch also still has the D3D_FEATURE_LEVEL_9_3 CopySubresourceRegion
path in TextureStorage11::copySubresourceLevel, which upstream had already
removed; its MakeValidSize call is converted to the new signature with
TextureType::_2D and a local depth/levelOffset (previously nullptr).

